# Disposable demo PRs

When you open a pull request against this demo as part of presenting (runbooks, field demos, Grok Build beats), name the **PR title and branch** so a later cleanup pass can delete them without guessing.

Do not use production-looking titles (`feat:`, `fix:`, a ticket id alone) for those PRs.

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — looks like a real ship
feat: add customer email editor on invoices
fix/filter-pills

# ✅ GOOD — obvious throwaway
[demo-delete-me] add customer email editor on invoices
demo/delete-me-filter-pills
```

Prefix the title with `[demo-delete-me]` (or equivalent) and put `demo/delete-me-` on the branch. This does not change whether you open a PR — only how you name presenting ones.
